commands) was denied approval in this environment — nothing was built, typechecked, linted, or tested; all gate results are unverified\\\",\\\"FC-0.6 boundary sabotage self-test and FC-0.7 gate self-tests (sacrificial failing test, edited Red-file manifest check) were NOT performed — they require running the real scripts\\\",\\\"Golden token counts asserted in smoke.test.ts (hello world = 2, empty = 0 under o200k_base) are from knowledge, not\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"persistedOutputPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/.claude/projects/-Users-leemoore-code-pi-long-horizon-liminal-context/7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e/tool-results/bqxq1s80y.txt\",\"persistedOutputSize\":291196}}\n421:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01ShpRbaHqtcXDBxUyEEKJr7\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"95\\t### Flow 5 — `idempotency.test.ts`\\n96\\t\\n97\\t| TC | Test | Setup | Key assertions |\\n98\\t|----|------|-------|----------------|\\n99\\t| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\\n100\\t| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\\n101\\t| TC-5.3 | cross-thread keys | same key, two threads | both record |\\n102\\t| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\\n103\\t| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\\n104\\t\\n105\\t### CLI process suite — `cli-process.test.ts` (verify-all only)\\n106\\t\\n107\\tRepresentative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\\n108\\t\\n109\\t## Architecture-Risk Tests (non-TC)\\n110\\t\\n111\\tBehaviors no TC names but the design promises; each exists because AC/TC mapping alone would miss it.\\n112\\t\\n113\\t| Risk | Test | Why TCs miss it |\\n114\\t|------|------|-----------------|\\n115\\t| Atomicity under mid-walk failure | induced failure inside the transaction (test seam closes handle) → read-back equals baseline | TC-4.3 covers validation rejection; this covers in-transaction failure |\\n116\\t| Restart survival | record batch, close handle, reopen → identical read-back including work items | NFR, no TC; the durability claim itself |\\n117\\t| Rejected batch takes no lock | concurrent open succeeds while rejection-path runs | design promise (pure validation before transaction), invisible to single-connection TCs |\\n118\\t| system_error rollback parity | storage failure mid-batch → rollback whole, `system_error` class | AC-4.6 is class-independent; TCs only exercise caller-error rejection |\\n119\\t| Fixture validity | builder defaults decode against real schemas | test substrate correctness, not product behavior |\\n120\\t| Boundary-check self-test | sabotage import fails the script | guards the guard |\\n121\\t| Verification gates fail correctly | failing test fails `verify`; edited Red file fails `green-verify` | proves the gates once (Chunk 0), then trusted |\\n122\\t| Registry lazy-init non-creation | reads against absent registry create no file | easy to get accidentally wrong with open-or-create storage helpers |\\n123\\t\\n124\\t## Coverage Summary\\n125\\t\\n126\\t| Flow | TCs | Supplemental | Est. tests |\\n127\\t|------|-----|--------------|-----------|\\n128\\t| 1 | 6 | lazy-init | 9 |\\n129\\t| 2 | 9 | — | 12 |\\n130\\t| 3 | 8 | golden suite | 14 |\\n131\\t| 4 | 5 | strictness, empty-fields | 10 |\\n132\\t| 5 | 5 | — | 7 |\\n133\\t| CLI process | — | boundary proofs | 6 |\\n134\\t| Architecture-risk | — | 8 risks | 9 |\\n135\\t| Chunk 0 smoke | — | rail, fixtures, tokenizer, gates | 5 |\\n136\\t| **Total** | **33** | | **~72** |\\n137\\t\\n138\\tWithin the epic's 60–72 estimate, at the top because architecture-risk tests are enumerated rather than folded in. Every TC from the epic appears exactly once as an owned row; the two cross-chunk deferrals (TC-1.4 → Chunk 2; TC-3.3/3.6 work halves → Chunk 5) are marked at their rows and owed by their receiving chunks.\\n139\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"afab5b83-5d2f-4f3e-b068-d25271daf8a0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T12:33:22.239Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/test-plan.md\",\"content\":\"### Flow 5 — `idempotency.test.ts`\\n\\n| TC | Test | Setup | Key assertions |\\n|----|------|-------|----------------|\\n| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\\n| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\\n| TC-5.3 | cross-thread keys | same key, two threads | both record |\\n| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\\n| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\\n\\n### CLI process suite — `cli-process.test.ts` (verify-all only)\\n\\nRepresentative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\\n\\n## Architecture-Risk Tests (non-TC)\\n\\nBehaviors no TC names but the design promises; each exists because AC/TC mapping alone would miss it.\\n\\n| Risk | Test | Why TCs miss it |\\n|------|------|-----------------|\\n| Atomicity under mid-walk failure | induced failure inside the transaction (test seam closes handle) → read-back equals baseline | TC-4.3 covers validation rejection; this covers in-transaction failure |\\n| Restart survival | record batch, close handle, reopen → identical read-back including work items | NFR, no TC; the durability claim itself |\\n| Rejected batch takes no lock | concurrent open succeeds while rejection-path runs | design promise (pure validation before transaction), invisible to single-connection TCs |\\n| system_error rollback parity | storage failure mid-batch → rollback whole, `system_error` class | AC-4.6 is class-independent; TCs only exercise caller-error rejection |\\n| Fixture validity | builder defaults decode against real schemas | test substrate correctness, not product behavior |\\n| Boundary-check self-test | sabotage import fails the script | guards the guard |\\n| Verification gates fail correctly | failing test fails `verify`; edited Red file fails `green-verify` | proves the gates once (Chunk 0), then trusted |\\n| Registry lazy-init non-creation | reads against absent registry create no file | easy to get accidentally wrong with open-or-create storage helpers |\\n\\n## Coverage Summary\\n\\n| Flow | TCs | Supplemental | Est. tests |\\n|------|-----|--------------|-----------|\\n| 1 | 6 | lazy-init | 9 |\\n| 2 | 9 | — | 12 |\\n| 3 | 8 | golden suite | 14 |\\n| 4 | 5 | strictness, empty-fields | 10 |\\n| 5 | 5 | — | 7 |\\n| CLI process | — | boundary proofs | 6 |\\n| Architecture-risk | — | 8 risks | 9 |\\n| Chunk 0 smoke | — | rail, fixtures, tokenizer, gates | 5 |\\n| **Total** | **33** | | **~72** |\\n\\nWithin the epic's 60–72 estimate, at the top because architecture-risk tests are enumerated rather than folded in. Every TC from the epic appears exactly once as an owned row; the two cross-chunk deferrals (TC-1.4 → Chunk 2; TC-3.3/3.6 work halves → Chunk 5) are marked at their rows and owed by their receiving chunks.\\n\",\"numLines\":45,\"startLine\":95,\"totalLines\":139}}}\n428:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FQdVY3BHKWTTfScadcs4Ab\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"560\\tlhc threads resolve --thread-id <id> [--registry <r>]\\n561\\tlhc threads list [--registry <r>]\\n562\\tlhc intake-stream message-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]   # events JSON array on stdin\\n563\\tlhc intake-stream list-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n564\\tlhc messages list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n565\\tlhc messages list-queued-work …\\n566\\tlhc turns list …\\n567\\tlhc turns list-queued-work …\\n568\\t```\\n569\\t\\n570\\tEvery command prints the SDK result (`value` or `error`) as JSON and exits 0/1. `message-events` refuses a TTY or empty stdin with `empty_stdin`. No CLI-only behavior exists; every command body is one SDK call plus rendering.\\n571\\t\\n572\\t---\\n573\\t\\n574\\t## Verification Gates\\n575\\t\\n576\\tFour script tiers, pinned here so every chunk's phases reference the same gates. All run from `packages/lhc`.\\n577\\t\\n578\\t| Script | Composition | Gate for |\\n579\\t|--------|-------------|----------|\\n580\\t| `red-verify` | build + typecheck + lint + boundary check (no behavior tests) | Red phase exit: skeleton compiles clean, failing tests are assertion failures, not wiring failures |\\n581\\t| `verify` | `red-verify` + full test suite | Green phase exit; the default local gate |\\n582\\t| `green-verify` | `verify` + test-immutability check (Red-phase test files unchanged since Red commit) | Green completion: behavior was implemented, tests were not edited to pass |\\n583\\t| `verify-all` | `verify` + CLI process-boundary suite | Chunk completion and CI |\\n584\\t\\n585\\tThe boundary check is `scripts/check-boundaries.mjs` (no imports into another domain's `internal/`; `tech-utils` and `shared` import no domain; fixtures directory exempt). Test immutability is enforced by comparing Red-committed test file hashes — Green may add new test files but may not modify Red's. The CLI process-boundary suite spawns the built `dist/cli.js`; it is the only suite excluded from plain `verify` because it needs a build artifact, and its absence from `verify` is labeled in output (`SKIP: cli-process suite — run verify-all`), never silent.\\n586\\t\\n587\\t## Work Breakdown\\n588\\t\\n589\\tSix chunks, tracking the epic's six stories one-to-one — the pipeline ordering that made the stories right makes the chunks right, and keeping the mapping 1:1 means story generation later inherits a pre-validated decomposition. Each chunk runs Skeleton → Red → Green internally. A chunk is complete when `verify-all` passes and its exit criteria hold.\\n590\\t\\n591\\tSubstrate maturity is the through-line: every chunk consumes the previous chunk's *real* artifacts — real registry, real thread files, real recorded events — never stand-ins. By Chunk 3, a test that wants \\\"a thread with six events\\\" creates it through the Chunk 2 surface, which is both less fixture code and a continuous re-verification of everything upstream.\\n592\\t\\n593\\t### Chunk 0: Foundations\\n594\\t\\n595\\t**Risk shape:** four archetypes in one — pure types (error/result vocabulary), fixtures (builders + temp stores), command rail (CLI routing with structured-failure stubs), substrate (sqlite open/migrate, boundary script, verification scripts).\\n596\\t**Delivers:** `shared/` complete (errors, context, storage); `tech-utils/token-counting` complete (it is pure and small — no reason to stub what costs nothing to finish); CLI rail routing all commands to fail-closed stubs returning `{ ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason: \\\"not implemented: <op>\\\" } }`; fixture builders (`validEvent(kind, overrides?)`, `eventBatch(…)`, temp-dir factory, `openRaw(path)` for below-SDK assertions); all four verification scripts runnable.\\n597\\t**Exit criteria:** `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; smoke tests prove the rail (help, unknown command, stub failure shape), fixture validity (builders satisfy the Flow 4 schemas once they exist — initially golden-shaped), tokenizer determinism (golden counts for known strings), and boundary script failure on a deliberate violation (test-only sabotage file, then removed).\\n598\\t**Architecture-risk tests:** boundary-check self-test; verification scripts fail when they should (a failing test fails `verify`; an edited Red file fails `green-verify` — proven once here with a sacrificial file, then trusted).\\n599\\t\\n600\\t### Chunk 1: Threads and Registry\\n601\\t\\n602\\t**Risk shape:** cross-database compensation; lazy initialization.\\n603\\t**Delivers:** Flow 1 complete — `newThread`, `resolve`, `listThreads`, `resolveThreadRef`, registry lazy-create, thread-file schema v1 (metadata row: thread id, created-at, `token_estimator`), compensation on registry failure; CLI `threads` commands live.\\n604\\t**Consumes:** Chunk 0's temp-dir factory, error vocabulary, CLI rail.\\n605\\t**Exit criteria:** TC-1.1–6 green via SDK; same six via CLI in-process; `new-thread` + `resolve` through the spawned binary in the process suite. Thread files created here are the substrate every later chunk builds on.\\n606\\t**Acceptance-risk reminder:** AC-1.6 is only half-testable until `message-events` exists (TC-1.4 sends batches); the chunk proves read-path equivalence and leaves a named deferral for Chunk 2 to close.\\n607\\t\\n608\\t### Chunk 2: Event Recording, Validation, Idempotency\\n609\\t\\n610\\t**Risk shape:** the strict boundary and the transaction skeleton — the two highest-risk seams in the epic land together here, deliberately, before any projection complicates the walk.\\n611\\t**Delivers:** Flow 4 complete (three-layer closed schemas, error mapping with `eventIndex`); Flow 5 complete at event level (skip set, `skipReason`, density of order numbers); Flow 2's recording half (the transaction, `MAX(event_order)` counter, event rows, walk-time result assembly minus messages/turns/work); `listEvents`; closes TC-1.4.\\n612\\t**Consumes:** real threads from Chunk 1.\\n613\\t**Exit criteria:** TC-4.1–5, TC-5.1–5 (asserting events only), TC-2.1, TC-2.8 green; the no-trace guarantee (TC-4.3) proven by read-back diff against a baseline thread; rejected batch takes no lock (observable: a concurrent open succeeds during a rejection-path test).\\n614\\t**Architecture-risk tests:** atomicity under induced mid-walk failure (close the db handle mid-transaction via test seam — rollback leaves read-back at baseline); restart survival (write, close handle, reopen, read-back identical).\\n615\\t\\n616\\t### Chunk 3: Message Projection and Tokens\\n617\\t\\n618\\t**Risk shape:** lowest in the epic — per-kind mapping against fixed contracts; the risk is fidelity, not logic.\\n619\\t**Delivers:** `createFromEvent` wired into the walk; per-kind block projection; token stamping via the Chunk 0 util; actor/harness carry; `listMessages`; deterministic `m<order>` ids; messageId in batch results.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"e13bc4cc-7a06-4e71-88b7-7b9c56dd0fce\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T12:33:23.066Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md\",\"content\":\"lhc threads resolve --thread-id <id> [--registry <r>]\\nlhc threads list [--registry <r>]\\nlhc intake-stream message-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]   # events JSON array on stdin\\nlhc intake-stream list-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\nlhc messages list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\nlhc messages list-queued-work …\\nlhc turns list …\\nlhc turns list-queued-work …\\n```\\n\\nEvery command prints the SDK result (`value` or `error`) as JSON and exits 0/1. `message-events` refuses a TTY or empty stdin with `empty_stdin`. No CLI-only behavior exists; every command body is one SDK call plus rendering.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verification Gates\\n\\nFour script tiers, pinned here so every chunk's phases reference the same gates. All run from `packages/lhc`.\\n\\n| Script | Composition | Gate for |\\n|--------|-------------|----------|\\n| `red-verify` | build + typecheck + lint + boundary check (no behavior tests) | Red phase exit: skeleton compiles clean, failing tests are assertion failures, not wiring failures |\\n| `verify` | `red-verify` + full test suite | Green phase exit; the default local gate |\\n| `green-verify` | `verify` + test-immutability check (Red-phase test files unchanged since Red commit) | Green completion: behavior was implemented, tests were not edited to pass |\\n| `verify-all` | `verify` + CLI process-boundary suite | Chunk completion and CI |\\n\\nThe boundary check is `scripts/check-boundaries.mjs` (no imports into another domain's `internal/`; `tech-utils` and `shared` import no domain; fixtures directory exempt). Test immutability is enforced by comparing Red-committed test file hashes — Green may add new test files but may not modify Red's. The CLI process-boundary suite spawns the built `dist/cli.js`; it is the only suite excluded from plain `verify` because it needs a build artifact, and its absence from `verify` is labeled in output (`SKIP: cli-process suite — run verify-all`), never silent.\\n\\n## Work Breakdown\\n\\nSix chunks, tracking the epic's six stories one-to-one — the pipeline ordering that made the stories right makes the chunks right, and keeping the mapping 1:1 means story generation later inherits a pre-validated decomposition. Each chunk runs Skeleton → Red → Green internally. A chunk is complete when `verify-all` passes and its exit criteria hold.\\n\\nSubstrate maturity is the through-line: every chunk consumes the previous chunk's *real* artifacts — real registry, real thread files, real recorded events — never stand-ins. By Chunk 3, a test that wants \\\"a thread with six events\\\" creates it through the Chunk 2 surface, which is both less fixture code and a continuous re-verification of everything upstream.\\n\\n### Chunk 0: Foundations\\n\\n**Risk shape:** four archetypes in one — pure types (error/result vocabulary), fixtures (builders + temp stores), command rail (CLI routing with structured-failure stubs), substrate (sqlite open/migrate, boundary script, verification scripts).\\n**Delivers:** `shared/` complete (errors, context, storage); `tech-utils/token-counting` complete (it is pure and small — no reason to stub what costs nothing to finish); CLI rail routing all commands to fail-closed stubs returning `{ ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason: \\\"not implemented: <op>\\\" } }`; fixture builders (`validEvent(kind, overrides?)`, `eventBatch(…)`, temp-dir factory, `openRaw(path)` for below-SDK assertions); all four verification scripts runnable.\\n**Exit criteria:** `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; smoke tests prove the rail (help, unknown command, stub failure shape), fixture validity (builders satisfy the Flow 4 schemas once they exist — initially golden-shaped), tokenizer determinism (golden counts for known strings), and boundary script failure on a deliberate violation (test-only sabotage file, then removed).\\n**Architecture-risk tests:** boundary-check self-test; verification scripts fail when they should (a failing test fails `verify`; an edited Red file fails `green-verify` — proven once here with a sacrificial file, then trusted).\\n\\n### Chunk 1: Threads and Registry\\n\\n**Risk shape:** cross-database compensation; lazy initialization.\\n**Delivers:** Flow 1 complete — `newThread`, `resolve`, `listThreads`, `resolveThreadRef`, registry lazy-create, thread-file schema v1 (metadata row: thread id, created-at, `token_estimator`), compensation on registry failure; CLI `threads` commands live.\\n**Consumes:** Chunk 0's temp-dir factory, error vocabulary, CLI rail.\\n**Exit criteria:** TC-1.1–6 green via SDK; same six via CLI in-process; `new-thread` + `resolve` through the spawned binary in the process suite. Thread files created here are the substrate every later chunk builds on.\\n**Acceptance-risk reminder:** AC-1.6 is only half-testable until `message-events` exists (TC-1.4 sends batches); the chunk proves read-path equivalence and leaves a named deferral for Chunk 2 to close.\\n\\n### Chunk 2: Event Recording, Validation, Idempotency\\n\\n**Risk shape:** the strict boundary and the transaction skeleton — the two highest-risk seams in the epic land together here, deliberately, before any projection complicates the walk.\\n**Delivers:** Flow 4 complete (three-layer closed schemas, error mapping with `eventIndex`); Flow 5 complete at event level (skip set, `skipReason`, density of order numbers); Flow 2's recording half (the transaction, `MAX(event_order)` counter, event rows, walk-time result assembly minus messages/turns/work); `listEvents`; closes TC-1.4.\\n**Consumes:** real threads from Chunk 1.\\n**Exit criteria:** TC-4.1–5, TC-5.1–5 (asserting events only), TC-2.1, TC-2.8 green; the no-trace guarantee (TC-4.3) proven by read-back diff against a baseline thread; rejected batch takes no lock (observable: a concurrent open succeeds during a rejection-path test).\\n**Architecture-risk tests:** atomicity under induced mid-walk failure (close the db handle mid-transaction via test seam — rollback leaves read-back at baseline); restart survival (write, close handle, reopen, read-back identical).\\n\\n### Chunk 3: Message Projection and Tokens\\n\\n**Risk shape:** lowest in the epic — per-kind mapping against fixed contracts; the risk is fidelity, not logic.\\n**Delivers:** `createFromEvent` wired into the walk; per-kind block projection; token stamping via the Chunk 0 util; actor/harness carry; `listMessages`; deterministic `m<order>` ids; messageId in batch results.\",\"numLines\":60,\"startLine\":560,\"totalLines\":653}}}\n449:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Find FC-0.7 references in test-plan and foundation story\"}},\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"c9278185-76eb-49c2-be7f-cc307b7d7364\"}\n451:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_011gu3TvvYycxeL69c2sWfHt\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01WkQ4vbGN7kyPjHv8dVvcLG\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"FC-0.7\\\\|FC-0\\\\.\\\" docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/test-plan.md docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md 2>/dev/null | head -40\",\"description\":\"Find FC-0.7 references in test-plan and foundation story\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4386,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":44338,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4386},\"output_tokens\":7,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"83fa6981-355f-4772-99e3-4f2fcb3fe9db\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbuavnCrFayC54tqGpPZF\"}\n454:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WkQ4vbGN7kyPjHv8dVvcLG\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:33:- **FC-0.1**: Package builds and typechecks strict; `red-verify` passes\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:34:- **FC-0.2**: `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; the CLI process suite's absence from plain `verify` prints a labeled skip, never silent\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:35:- **FC-0.3**: CLI responds to `--help`; unknown commands exit non-zero with a structured error; every planned command routes to a fail-closed stub with the exact stub error shape\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:36:- **FC-0.4**: Fixture builders produce inputs that decode clean against the boundary schemas once Story 2 lands (golden-shaped until then); building an invalid kind/payload pairing requires an explicit cast at the call site\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:37:- **FC-0.5**: `estimateTokens` returns golden counts for known strings; same input, same count, every run\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:38:- **FC-0.6**: Boundary check fails on a deliberate sabotage import (test-only file, then removed) and passes on the clean tree\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:39:- **FC-0.7**: Gate self-test: a sacrificial failing test fails `verify`; an edited Red-phase test file fails `green-verify` — proven once here, then trusted\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:59:- Gate self-test (FC-0.7) is load-bearing: an unproven gate is an assumed gate.\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:88:No epic TCs. Story-owned checks are FC-0.1 through FC-0.7 (numbered in Acceptance Criteria above):\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:92:| FC-0.1 | `pnpm run red-verify` | build + typecheck + lint + boundaries, clean |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:93:| FC-0.2 | `pnpm run verify-all` | passes with zero behavior tests; labeled CLI-suite skip under `verify` |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:94:| FC-0.3 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | help, unknown command, stub failure shape |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:95:| FC-0.4 | `test/fixtures.test.ts` | builder defaults golden-shaped; invalid pairings need explicit casts |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:96:| FC-0.5 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | golden token counts, repeated runs identical |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:97:| FC-0.6 | boundary-check self-test | sabotage import fails, clean tree passes |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:98:| FC-0.7 | gate self-test (recorded, then removed) | failing test fails `verify`; edited Red file fails `green-verify` |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:105:| Boundary check guards itself | self-test in FC-0.6 | the guard fails when violated | a silently broken guard passes every later story while enforcing nothing |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:106:| Gates fail correctly | FC-0.7 procedure | gates catch what they exist to catch | a gate that cannot fail certifies nothing |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:145:- [ ] Smoke suite green (4–6 tests) covering FC-0.1 through FC-0.7; gate self-test (FC-0.7) performed and recorded\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"74ad823c-eddb-49aa-8ed0-6c1a3454eb7b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T12:33:33.458Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:33:- **FC-0.1**: Package builds and typechecks strict; `red-verify` passes\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:34:- **FC-0.2**: `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; the CLI process suite's absence from plain `verify` prints a labeled skip, never silent\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:35:- **FC-0.3**: CLI responds to `--help`; unknown commands exit non-zero with a structured error; every planned command routes to a fail-closed stub with the exact stub error shape\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:36:- **FC-0.4**: Fixture builders produce inputs that decode clean against the boundary schemas once Story 2 lands (golden-shaped until then); building an invalid kind/payload pairing requires an explicit cast at the call site\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:37:- **FC-0.5**: `estimateTokens` returns golden counts for known strings; same input, same count, every run\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:38:- **FC-0.6**: Boundary check fails on a deliberate sabotage import (test-only file, then removed) and passes on the clean tree\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:39:- **FC-0.7**: Gate self-test: a sacrificial failing test fails `verify`; an edited Red-phase test file fails `green-verify` — proven once here, then trusted\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:59:- Gate self-test (FC-0.7) is load-bearing: an unproven gate is an assumed gate.\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:88:No epic TCs. Story-owned checks are FC-0.1 through FC-0.7 (numbered in Acceptance Criteria above):\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:92:| FC-0.1 | `pnpm run red-verify` | build + typecheck + lint + boundaries, clean |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:93:| FC-0.2 | `pnpm run verify-all` | passes with zero behavior tests; labeled CLI-suite skip under `verify` |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:94:| FC-0.3 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | help, unknown command, stub failure shape |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:95:| FC-0.4 | `test/fixtures.test.ts` | builder defaults golden-shaped; invalid pairings need explicit casts |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:96:| FC-0.5 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | golden token counts, repeated runs identical |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:97:| FC-0.6 | boundary-check self-test | sabotage import fails, clean tree passes |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:98:| FC-0.7 | gate self-test (recorded, then removed) | failing test fails `verify`; edited Red file fails `green-verify` |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:105:| Boundary check guards itself | self-test in FC-0.6 | the guard fails when violated | a silently broken guard passes every later story while enforcing nothing |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:106:| Gates fail correctly | FC-0.7 procedure | gates catch what they exist to catch | a gate that cannot fail certifies nothing |\\ndocs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:145:- [ ] Smoke suite green (4–6 tests) covering FC-0.1 through FC-0.7; gate self-test (FC-0.7) performed and recorded\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n471:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_012rzs49YvquYuDcifTUhoBN\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Story 0: Package Foundations\\n2\\t\\n3\\t### Summary\\n4\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n5\\t\\n6\\tThe walking skeleton everything else lands on: package scaffold, error/result vocabulary, fixture builders, CLI rail with fail-closed stubs, and the four verification gates.\\n7\\t\\n8\\t### Description\\n9\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n10\\t\\n11\\t**User Profile** (from epic): Primary user is the harness integrator wiring a harness to the SDK; agents and developers drive the CLI during integration and verification. This story serves them indirectly — it builds the structure every later story adds behavior to.\\n12\\t\\n13\\t**Objective:** Every later story adds behavior to a structure that already builds, runs, and fails closed. After this story, the package compiles strict, the CLI routes every planned command to a typed structured failure, fixtures produce valid inputs, and all four verification gates run and provably fail when they should.\\n14\\t\\n15\\t**Scope — in:**\\n16\\t- Package scaffold per the tech design's module structure: `domains/` (threads, intake-stream, messages, turns — surface + `internal/`), `tech-utils/` (work-queue, token-counting), `shared/` (errors, context, storage), `cli/`, `sdk.ts`\\n17\\t- `shared/errors.ts` complete: `ErrorClass`, `ErrorCode`, `ErrorResult`, `OpResult<T>` exactly as the tech design's Interfaces section defines them\\n18\\t- `tech-utils/token-counting` complete (pure and small): `estimateTokens`, `TOKEN_ESTIMATOR_ID = \\\"js-tiktoken:o200k_base\\\"`\\n19\\t- CLI rail: command routing for all planned commands, each landing on a fail-closed stub returning `{ ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason: \\\"not implemented: <op>\\\" } }`; `--help`; unknown-command handling; JSON rendering; exit codes\\n20\\t- Fixture builders: `tempStore()`, `validEvent(kind, overrides?)` returning the discriminated `MessageEventInput` member for its kind, `eventBatch(kinds[])`, `conversationTurn()`, `openRaw(path)`, `corruptTwoOpenTurns(path)` (shape only; meaningful from Story 4)\\n21\\t- Verification gates: `red-verify`, `verify`, `green-verify`, `verify-all` runnable; `scripts/check-boundaries.mjs` enforcing import rules (fixtures exempt); CLI process suite scaffold with labeled skip under plain `verify`\\n22\\t- Smoke tests proving the rail, fixture validity, tokenizer determinism, and gate correctness\\n23\\t\\n24\\t**Scope — out:** All product behavior. No thread creation, no intake, no projection, no turns, no work items. Stubs fail closed; nothing fakes success.\\n25\\t\\n26\\t**Dependencies:** None. First story.\\n27\\t\\n28\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\n29\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n30\\t\\n31\\tThis story owns no epic ACs. Its acceptance is the numbered foundation criteria below (FC ids are this story's receipt vocabulary, mirroring AC/TC structure for enrichment and closeout):\\n32\\t\\n33\\t- **FC-0.1**: Package builds and typechecks strict; `red-verify` passes\\n34\\t- **FC-0.2**: `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; the CLI process suite's absence from plain `verify` prints a labeled skip, never silent\\n35\\t- **FC-0.3**: CLI responds to `--help`; unknown commands exit non-zero with a structured error; every planned command routes to a fail-closed stub with the exact stub error shape\\n36\\t- **FC-0.4**: Fixture builders produce inputs that decode clean against the boundary schemas once Story 2 lands (golden-shaped until then); building an invalid kind/payload pairing requires an explicit cast at the call site\\n37\\t- **FC-0.5**: `estimateTokens` returns golden counts for known strings; same input, same count, every run\\n38\\t- **FC-0.6**: Boundary check fails on a deliberate sabotage import (test-only file, then removed) and passes on the clean tree\\n39\\t- **FC-0.7**: Gate self-test: a sacrificial failing test fails `verify`; an edited Red-phase test file fails `green-verify` — proven once here, then trusted\\n40\\t\\n41\\t### Technical Design\\n42\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n43\\t\\n44\\t#### Architecture Context\\n45\\t\\n46\\tThis story builds the structure every other story lands behavior in: the domain-surface module tree with enforced import boundaries, the error/result vocabulary every operation speaks, the fixture builders every test arranges with, and the four verification gates every phase exits through. Nothing here is product behavior — the CLI routes to fail-closed stubs and the SDK exports types and one finished util (token counting, which is pure and costs nothing to complete now).\\n47\\t\\n48\\tThe gates are the real deliverable. Red/Green discipline in Stories 1–5 leans on `green-verify` catching edited tests and `verify` catching real failures — so this story must *prove the gates fail correctly*, once, with sacrificial files, rather than assume they do.\\n49\\t\\n50\\t#### Build Strategy\\n51\\t\\n52\\tStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\n53\\t\\n54\\tReason:\\n55\\t- Mostly scaffold with obvious shape; TDD against stubs that intentionally fail would be circular.\\n56\\t\\n57\\tRisk Reminders:\\n58\\t- Stubs must fail closed with the exact typed error shape — a stub returning fake success poisons every later story's red phase.\\n59\\t- Gate self-test (FC-0.7) is load-bearing: an unproven gate is an assumed gate.\\n60\\t- The boundary script must fail on a real sabotage import before it is trusted to pass the clean tree.\\n61\\t\\n62\\t#### Implementation Targets\\n63\\t\\n64\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\n65\\t|------|-----------------|\\n66\\t| Module tree | `src/domains/{threads,intake-stream,messages,turns}/{index.ts,internal/}`, `src/tech-utils/{work-queue,token-counting}/`, `src/shared/`, `src/cli/`, `src/sdk.ts` |\\n67\\t| Error vocabulary | `src/shared/errors.ts` |\\n68\\t| Operation context type | `src/shared/context.ts` |\\n69\\t| Storage helpers | `src/shared/storage.ts` (open, WAL pragmas, migration runner) |\\n70\\t| Token counting | `src/tech-utils/token-counting/index.ts` |\\n71\\t| CLI rail | `src/cli/index.ts`, `src/cli/render.ts` |\\n72\\t| Fixtures | `test/fixtures/` (builders, temp stores, `corrupt.ts`, `openRaw`) |\\n73\\t| Gates | `scripts/check-boundaries.mjs`, package scripts `red-verify`/`verify`/`green-verify`/`verify-all` |\\n74\\t| Smoke tests | `test/smoke.test.ts`, `test/fixtures.test.ts` (names inferred; Chunk 0 scope) |\\n75\\t\\n76\\t#### Design References\\n77\\t\\n78\\t- [02-tech-design.md §Module Structure](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:72), lines 72–119\\n79\\t- [02-tech-design.md §Design Decision 4: Error representation](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:157), lines 157–176\\n80\\t- [02-tech-design.md §Interfaces: Shared vocabulary](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:372), lines 372–407\\n81\\t- [02-tech-design.md §Verification Gates](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:574), lines 574–586\\n82\\t- [02-tech-design.md §Chunk 0: Foundations](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:593), lines 593–599\\n83\\t- [03-test-plan.md §Testing Strategy](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/03-test-plan.md:5), lines 5–23\\n84\\t- [03-test-plan.md §Fixture Contracts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/03-test-plan.md:24), lines 24–39\\n85\\t\\n86\\t#### Test Mapping\\n87\\t\\n88\\tNo epic TCs. Story-owned checks are FC-0.1 through FC-0.7 (numbered in Acceptance Criteria above):\\n89\\t\\n90\\t| FC | Test File / Check | Description |\\n91\\t|----|-------------------|-------------|\\n92\\t| FC-0.1 | `pnpm run red-verify` | build + typecheck + lint + boundaries, clean |\\n93\\t| FC-0.2 | `pnpm run verify-all` | passes with zero behavior tests; labeled CLI-suite skip under `verify` |\\n94\\t| FC-0.3 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | help, unknown command, stub failure shape |\\n95\\t| FC-0.4 | `test/fixtures.test.ts` | builder defaults golden-shaped; invalid pairings need explicit casts |\\n96\\t| FC-0.5 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | golden token counts, repeated runs identical |\\n97\\t| FC-0.6 | boundary-check self-test | sabotage import fails, clean tree passes |\\n98\\t| FC-0.7 | gate self-test (recorded, then removed) | failing test fails `verify`; edited Red file fails `green-verify` |\\n99\\t\\n100\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n101\\t\\n102\\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n103\\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n104\\t| Fixture validity | `test/fixtures.test.ts` | builders produce valid default states | test substrate correctness, not product behavior — no TC names it |\\n105\\t| Boundary check guards itself | self-test in FC-0.6 | the guard fails when violated | a silently broken guard passes every later story while enforcing nothing |\\n106\\t| Gates fail correctly | FC-0.7 procedure | gates catch what they exist to catch | a gate that cannot fail certifies nothing |\\n107\\t\\n108\\t#### Technical Notes\\n109\\t\\n110\\t- Error result vocabulary (contractual for every later story): `errorClass` ∈ `caller_error` / `state_corruption` / `system_error`; stable `code` set `path_exists`, `thread_not_found`, `invalid_event`, `empty_batch`, `empty_stdin`, `turn_state_corrupt`, `storage_failure`; `eventIndex` on batch validation failures; `reason` human-readable, machine logic switches on `code`.\\n111\\t- `empty_stdin` is CLI-adapter-only, emitted before any SDK call. Operational failures return as `OpResult` errors, never thrown; programmer bugs may throw and are not contract outcomes.\\n112\\t- CLI conventions: every command body is one SDK call plus rendering; JSON output matching SDK shapes; exit 0/1.\\n113\\t- `shared/` is mechanism-only: primitive cross-cutting identifiers and the result vocabulary, no domain workflows, row shapes, or policies.\\n114\\t\\n115\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n116\\t\\n117\\t- Stub error shape is asserted exactly (`system_error` / `storage_failure` / `not implemented: <op>`) — not just \\\"an error happened.\\\"\\n118\\t- The gate self-test must use real sacrificial files run through the real scripts; a gate \\\"reviewed as correct\\\" is not a gate proven to fail.\\n119\\t- Fixture builders return the discriminated `MessageEventInput` member per kind — invalid kind/payload pairings must be compile errors, demonstrated by an `@ts-expect-error` case, not convention.\\n120\\t\\n121\\t#### Production Path Proof\\n122\\t\\n123\\t- Entrypoint: `dist/cli.js` via the `lhc` bin; SDK via package exports.\\n124\\t- Registration/default path: `package.json` `bin` + `exports` maps; CLI router reaches every planned command.\\n125\\t- Evidence: process-suite legs (`--help`, unknown command, stub shape) spawn the built binary; `verify-all` includes them.\\n126\\t\\n127\\t#### Verification\\n128\\t\\n129\\t- Targeted: `pnpm test -- test/smoke.test.ts test/fixtures.test.ts`\\n130\\t- Story gate: `pnpm run green-verify`\\n131\\t- Epic gate: `pnpm run verify-all`\\n132\\t\\n133\\t#### Spec Deviations\\n134\\t\\n135\\tNone.\\n136\\t\\n137\\t### Definition of Done\\n138\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n139\\t\\n140\\t- [ ] Module tree matches the tech design's structure; every file belongs to one domain, util, shared, or cli\\n141\\t- [ ] `shared/errors.ts` and `tech-utils/token-counting` complete and exported\\n142\\t- [ ] All planned CLI commands route to fail-closed stubs; no stub returns fake success\\n143\\t- [ ] Fixture builders implemented; `corruptTwoOpenTurns` is the only below-SDK writer and lives in the exempt fixtures directory\\n144\\t- [ ] All four verification scripts runnable from `packages/lhc`; boundary check wired into `verify`\\n145\\t- [ ] Smoke suite green (4–6 tests) covering FC-0.1 through FC-0.7; gate self-test (FC-0.7) performed and recorded\\n146\\t- [ ] `verify-all` passes end to end\\n147\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"e7323662-8869-4942-8ae9-811340d461e9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T12:33:37.501Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md\",\"content\":\"# Story 0: Package Foundations\\n\\n### Summary\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n\\nThe walking skeleton everything else lands on: package scaffold, error/result vocabulary, fixture builders, CLI rail with fail-closed stubs, and the four verification gates.\\n\\n### Description\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n\\n**User Profile** (from epic): Primary user is the harness integrator wiring a harness to the SDK; agents and developers drive the CLI during integration and verification. This story serves them indirectly — it builds the structure every later story adds behavior to.\\n\\n**Objective:** Every later story adds behavior to a structure that already builds, runs, and fails closed. After this story, the package compiles strict, the CLI routes every planned command to a typed structured failure, fixtures produce valid inputs, and all four verification gates run and provably fail when they should.\\n\\n**Scope — in:**\\n- Package scaffold per the tech design's module structure: `domains/` (threads, intake-stream, messages, turns — surface + `internal/`), `tech-utils/` (work-queue, token-counting), `shared/` (errors, context, storage), `cli/`, `sdk.ts`\\n- `shared/errors.ts` complete: `ErrorClass`, `ErrorCode`, `ErrorResult`, `OpResult<T>` exactly as the tech design's Interfaces section defines them\\n- `tech-utils/token-counting` complete (pure and small): `estimateTokens`, `TOKEN_ESTIMATOR_ID = \\\"js-tiktoken:o200k_base\\\"`\\n- CLI rail: command routing for all planned commands, each landing on a fail-closed stub returning `{ ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason: \\\"not implemented: <op>\\\" } }`; `--help`; unknown-command handling; JSON rendering; exit codes\\n- Fixture builders: `tempStore()`, `validEvent(kind, overrides?)` returning the discriminated `MessageEventInput` member for its kind, `eventBatch(kinds[])`, `conversationTurn()`, `openRaw(path)`, `corruptTwoOpenTurns(path)` (shape only; meaningful from Story 4)\\n- Verification gates: `red-verify`, `verify`, `green-verify`, `verify-all` runnable; `scripts/check-boundaries.mjs` enforcing import rules (fixtures exempt); CLI process suite scaffold with labeled skip under plain `verify`\\n- Smoke tests proving the rail, fixture validity, tokenizer determinism, and gate correctness\\n\\n**Scope — out:** All product behavior. No thread creation, no intake, no projection, no turns, no work items. Stubs fail closed; nothing fakes success.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** None. First story.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n\\nThis story owns no epic ACs. Its acceptance is the numbered foundation criteria below (FC ids are this story's receipt vocabulary, mirroring AC/TC structure for enrichment and closeout):\\n\\n- **FC-0.1**: Package builds and typechecks strict; `red-verify` passes\\n- **FC-0.2**: `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; the CLI process suite's absence from plain `verify` prints a labeled skip, never silent\\n- **FC-0.3**: CLI responds to `--help`; unknown commands exit non-zero with a structured error; every planned command routes to a fail-closed stub with the exact stub error shape\\n- **FC-0.4**: Fixture builders produce inputs that decode clean against the boundary schemas once Story 2 lands (golden-shaped until then); building an invalid kind/payload pairing requires an explicit cast at the call site\\n- **FC-0.5**: `estimateTokens` returns golden counts for known strings; same input, same count, every run\\n- **FC-0.6**: Boundary check fails on a deliberate sabotage import (test-only file, then removed) and passes on the clean tree\\n- **FC-0.7**: Gate self-test: a sacrificial failing test fails `verify`; an edited Red-phase test file fails `green-verify` — proven once here, then trusted\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n\\n#### Architecture Context\\n\\nThis story builds the structure every other story lands behavior in: the domain-surface module tree with enforced import boundaries, the error/result vocabulary every operation speaks, the fixture builders every test arranges with, and the four verification gates every phase exits through. Nothing here is product behavior — the CLI routes to fail-closed stubs and the SDK exports types and one finished util (token counting, which is pure and costs nothing to complete now).\\n\\nThe gates are the real deliverable. Red/Green discipline in Stories 1–5 leans on `green-verify` catching edited tests and `verify` catching real failures — so this story must *prove the gates fail correctly*, once, with sacrificial files, rather than assume they do.\\n\\n#### Build Strategy\\n\\nStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\n\\nReason:\\n- Mostly scaffold with obvious shape; TDD against stubs that intentionally fail would be circular.\\n\\nRisk Reminders:\\n- Stubs must fail closed with the exact typed error shape — a stub returning fake success poisons every later story's red phase.\\n- Gate self-test (FC-0.7) is load-bearing: an unproven gate is an assumed gate.\\n- The boundary script must fail on a real sabotage import before it is trusted to pass the clean tree.\\n\\n#### Implementation Targets\\n\\n| Area | Files / Modules |\\n|------|-----------------|\\n| Module tree | `src/domains/{threads,intake-stream,messages,turns}/{index.ts,internal/}`, `src/tech-utils/{work-queue,token-counting}/`, `src/shared/`, `src/cli/`, `src/sdk.ts` |\\n| Error vocabulary | `src/shared/errors.ts` |\\n| Operation context type | `src/shared/context.ts` |\\n| Storage helpers | `src/shared/storage.ts` (open, WAL pragmas, migration runner) |\\n| Token counting | `src/tech-utils/token-counting/index.ts` |\\n| CLI rail | `src/cli/index.ts`, `src/cli/render.ts` |\\n| Fixtures | `test/fixtures/` (builders, temp stores, `corrupt.ts`, `openRaw`) |\\n| Gates | `scripts/check-boundaries.mjs`, package scripts `red-verify`/`verify`/`green-verify`/`verify-all` |\\n| Smoke tests | `test/smoke.test.ts`, `test/fixtures.test.ts` (names inferred; Chunk 0 scope) |\\n\\n#### Design References\\n\\n- [02-tech-design.md §Module Structure](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:72), lines 72–119\\n- [02-tech-design.md §Design Decision 4: Error representation](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:157), lines 157–176\\n- [02-tech-design.md §Interfaces: Shared vocabulary](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:372), lines 372–407\\n- [02-tech-design.md §Verification Gates](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:574), lines 574–586\\n- [02-tech-design.md §Chunk 0: Foundations](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/02-tech-design.md:593), lines 593–599\\n- [03-test-plan.md §Testing Strategy](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/03-test-plan.md:5), lines 5–23\\n- [03-test-plan.md §Fixture Contracts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/03-test-plan.md:24), lines 24–39\\n\\n#### Test Mapping\\n\\nNo epic TCs. Story-owned checks are FC-0.1 through FC-0.7 (numbered in Acceptance Criteria above):\\n\\n| FC | Test File / Check | Description |\\n|----|-------------------|-------------|\\n| FC-0.1 | `pnpm run red-verify` | build + typecheck + lint + boundaries, clean |\\n| FC-0.2 | `pnpm run verify-all` | passes with zero behavior tests; labeled CLI-suite skip under `verify` |\\n| FC-0.3 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | help, unknown command, stub failure shape |\\n| FC-0.4 | `test/fixtures.test.ts` | builder defaults golden-shaped; invalid pairings need explicit casts |\\n| FC-0.5 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | golden token counts, repeated runs identical |\\n| FC-0.6 | boundary-check self-test | sabotage import fails, clean tree passes |\\n| FC-0.7 | gate self-test (recorded, then removed) | failing test fails `verify`; edited Red file fails `green-verify` |\\n\\n#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n| Fixture validity | `test/fixtures.test.ts` | builders produce valid default states | test substrate correctness, not product behavior — no TC names it |\\n| Boundary check guards itself | self-test in FC-0.6 | the guard fails when violated | a silently broken guard passes every later story while enforcing nothing |\\n| Gates fail correctly | FC-0.7 procedure | gates catch what they exist to catch | a gate that cannot fail certifies nothing |\\n\\n#### Technical Notes\\n\\n- Error result vocabulary (contractual for every later story): `errorClass` ∈ `caller_error` / `state_corruption` / `system_error`; stable `code` set `path_exists`, `thread_not_found`, `invalid_event`, `empty_batch`, `empty_stdin`, `turn_state_corrupt`, `storage_failure`; `eventIndex` on batch validation failures; `reason` human-readable, machine logic switches on `code`.\\n- `empty_stdin` is CLI-adapter-only, emitted before any SDK call. Operational failures return as `OpResult` errors, never thrown; programmer bugs may throw and are not contract outcomes.\\n- CLI conventions: every command body is one SDK call plus rendering; JSON output matching SDK shapes; exit 0/1.\\n- `shared/` is mechanism-only: primitive cross-cutting identifiers and the result vocabulary, no domain workflows, row shapes, or policies.\\n\\n#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n\\n- Stub error shape is asserted exactly (`system_error` / `storage_failure` / `not implemented: <op>`) — not just \\\"an error happened.\\\"\\n- The gate self-test must use real sacrificial files run through the real scripts; a gate \\\"reviewed as correct\\\" is not a gate proven to fail.\\n- Fixture builders return the discriminated `MessageEventInput` member per kind — invalid kind/payload pairings must be compile errors, demonstrated by an `@ts-expect-error` case, not convention.\\n\\n#### Production Path Proof\\n\\n- Entrypoint: `dist/cli.js` via the `lhc` bin; SDK via package exports.\\n- Registration/default path: `package.json` `bin` + `exports` maps; CLI router reaches every planned command.\\n- Evidence: process-suite legs (`--help`, unknown command, stub shape) spawn the built binary; `verify-all` includes them.\\n\\n#### Verification\\n\\n- Targeted: `pnpm test -- test/smoke.test.ts test/fixtures.test.ts`\\n- Story gate: `pnpm run green-verify`\\n- Epic gate: `pnpm run verify-all`\\n\\n#### Spec Deviations\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Definition of Done\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n\\n- [ ] Module tree matches the tech design's structure; every file belongs to one domain, util, shared, or cli\\n- [ ] `shared/errors.ts` and `tech-utils/token-counting` complete and exported\\n- [ ] All planned CLI commands route to fail-closed stubs; no stub returns fake success\\n- [ ] Fixture builders implemented; `corruptTwoOpenTurns` is the only below-SDK writer and lives in the exempt fixtures directory\\n- [ ] All four verification scripts runnable from `packages/lhc`; boundary check wired into `verify`\\n- [ ] Smoke suite green (4–6 tests) covering FC-0.1 through FC-0.7; gate self-test (FC-0.7) performed and recorded\\n- [ ] `verify-all` passes end to end\\n\",\"numLines\":147,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":147}}}\n485:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{\\\"command\\\": \\\"echo \\\\\\\"=== red-manifest ===\\\\\\\"; cat test/red-manifest.json\"}},\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"60afe526-d80f-497e-b3e9-ff5349870b39\"}\n486:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\" 2>/dev/null || echo \\\\\\\"(no red-manifest.json)\\\\\\\"; echo; echo \\\\\\\"=== test dir ===\\\\\\\"; ls -la test/; echo \\\\\\\"\"}},\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"e1f08d06-68e3-491d-8d00-eb966f6c74e3\"}\n487:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"=== record-red-manifest.mjs ===\\\\\\\"; cat scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs\"}},\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"99cc372c-66de-4d69-af01-33300b66497e\"}\n491:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01K6PAhU6VDnraZA1CLtJd1n\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_0199pQUhLHx4v4qS5ckFgzcM\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== red-manifest ===\\\"; cat test/red-manifest.json 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"(no red-manifest.json)\\\"; echo; echo \\\"=== test dir ===\\\"; ls -la test/; echo \\\"=== record-red-manifest.mjs ===\\\"; cat scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs\",\"description\":\"Check red-manifest, test dir, record script\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5113,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":50927,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":5113},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"eb3e15af-e8d3-4460-a7f5-1dd49ce83fe9\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cbuawqxqwoj7rUUozFzFK\"}\n494:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_0199pQUhLHx4v4qS5ckFgzcM\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"=== red-manifest ===\\n(no red-manifest.json)\\n\\n=== test dir ===\\ntotal 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 leemoore  staff   192 Jun 10 08:28 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 13 leemoore  staff   416 Jun 10 08:24 ..\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 leemoore  staff  1745 Jun 10 08:23 cli-process.test.ts\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 leemoore  staff   128 Jun 10 08:20 fixtures\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 leemoore  staff  3576 Jun 10 08:23 fixtures.test.ts\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 leemoore  staff  3808 Jun 10 08:23 smoke.test.ts\\n=== record-red-manifest.mjs ===\\n#!/usr/bin/env node\\n// Records sha256 hashes of Red-phase test files into test/red-manifest.json.\\n// Usage: node scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs test/foo.test.ts [more files...]\\nimport { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\n\\nconst pkgRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\"..\\\");\\nconst manifestPath = path.join(pkgRoot, \\\"test\\\", \\\"red-manifest.json\\\");\\n\\nconst files = process.argv.slice(2);\\nif (files.length === 0) {\\n  console.error(\\\"usage: node scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs <test file> [...]\\\");\\n  process.exit(1);\\n}\\n\\nconst manifest = existsSync(manifestPath)\\n  ? JSON.parse(readFileSync(manifestPath, \\\"utf8\\\"))\\n  : { files: {} };\\nmanifest.files ??= {};\\n\\nfor (const file of files) {\\n  const rel = path.isAbsolute(file) ? path.relative(pkgRoot, file) : file;\\n  const full = path.join(pkgRoot, rel);\\n  manifest.files[rel] = createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(readFileSync(full)).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n  console.log(`recorded ${rel}`);\\n}\\n\\nwriteFileSync(manifestPath, `${JSON.stringify(manifest, null, 2)}\\\\n`);\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"dfa0c9c0-aef1-48f2-a563-d6bacc5b7983\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T12:33:43.831Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"=== red-manifest ===\\n(no red-manifest.json)\\n\\n=== test dir ===\\ntotal 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 leemoore  staff   192 Jun 10 08:28 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 13 leemoore  staff   416 Jun 10 08:24 ..\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 leemoore  staff  1745 Jun 10 08:23 cli-process.test.ts\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 leemoore  staff   128 Jun 10 08:20 fixtures\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 leemoore  staff  3576 Jun 10 08:23 fixtures.test.ts\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 leemoore  staff  3808 Jun 10 08:23 smoke.test.ts\\n=== record-red-manifest.mjs ===\\n#!/usr/bin/env node\\n// Records sha256 hashes of Red-phase test files into test/red-manifest.json.\\n// Usage: node scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs test/foo.test.ts [more files...]\\nimport { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\n\\nconst pkgRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\"..\\\");\\nconst manifestPath = path.join(pkgRoot, \\\"test\\\", \\\"red-manifest.json\\\");\\n\\nconst files = process.argv.slice(2);\\nif (files.length === 0) {\\n  console.error(\\\"usage: node scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs <test file> [...]\\\");\\n  process.exit(1);\\n}\\n\\nconst manifest = existsSync(manifestPath)\\n  ? JSON.parse(readFileSync(manifestPath, \\\"utf8\\\"))\\n  : { files: {} };\\nmanifest.files ??= {};\\n\\nfor (const file of files) {\\n  const rel = path.isAbsolute(file) ? path.relative(pkgRoot, file) : file;\\n  const full = path.join(pkgRoot, rel);\\n  manifest.files[rel] = createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(readFileSync(full)).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n  console.log(`recorded ${rel}`);\\n}\\n\\nwriteFileSync(manifestPath, `${JSON.stringify(manifest, null, 2)}\\\\n`);\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n514:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_013PYYP2dhuxMR9o5k66zuiH\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// CLI process-boundary suite: spawns the built dist/cli.js. Runs under\\n2\\t// verify-all only (needs a build artifact); plain verify announces the skip.\\n3\\timport { spawnSync } from \\\"node:child_process\\\";\\n4\\timport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n5\\timport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\n6\\timport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\n7\\timport { describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n8\\t\\n9\\tconst cliPath = path.resolve(\\n10\\t  path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)),\\n11\\t  \\\"../dist/cli.js\\\",\\n12\\t);\\n13\\t\\n14\\tfunction runBinary(args: string[]): {\\n15\\t  status: number | null;\\n16\\t  stdout: string;\\n17\\t  stderr: string;\\n18\\t} {\\n19\\t  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [cliPath, ...args], {\\n20\\t    encoding: \\\"utf8\\\",\\n21\\t  });\\n22\\t  return { status: result.status, stdout: result.stdout, stderr: result.stderr };\\n23\\t}\\n24\\t\\n25\\tdescribe(\\\"FC-0.3 (process boundary): built binary\\\", () => {\\n26\\t  it(\\\"dist/cli.js exists (build ran before this suite)\\\", () => {\\n27\\t    expect(existsSync(cliPath)).toBe(true);\\n28\\t  });\\n29\\t\\n30\\t  it(\\\"--help exits 0 with usage on stdout\\\", () => {\\n31\\t    const result = runBinary([\\\"--help\\\"]);\\n32\\t    expect(result.status).toBe(0);\\n33\\t    expect(result.stdout).toContain(\\\"Usage:\\\");\\n34\\t  });\\n35\\t\\n36\\t  it(\\\"unknown command exits 1 with structured JSON\\\", () => {\\n37\\t    const result = runBinary([\\\"nonsense\\\"]);\\n38\\t    expect(result.status).toBe(1);\\n39\\t    const parsed = JSON.parse(result.stdout) as { ok: boolean };\\n40\\t    expect(parsed.ok).toBe(false);\\n41\\t  });\\n42\\t\\n43\\t  it(\\\"a planned command reaches its fail-closed stub through the real binary\\\", () => {\\n44\\t    const result = runBinary([\\\"threads\\\", \\\"list\\\"]);\\n45\\t    expect(result.status).toBe(1);\\n46\\t    expect(JSON.parse(result.stdout)).toEqual({\\n47\\t      ok: false,\\n48\\t      error: {\\n49\\t        errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\",\\n50\\t        code: \\\"storage_failure\\\",\\n51\\t        reason: \\\"not implemented: threads.list\\\",\\n52\\t      },\\n53\\t    });\\n54\\t  });\\n55\\t});\\n56\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"ca777910-75db-45e0-b07f-b6119e93ba8d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T12:33:47.287Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/cli-process.test.ts\",\"content\":\"// CLI process-boundary suite: spawns the built dist/cli.js. Runs under\\n// verify-all only (needs a build artifact); plain verify announces the skip.\\nimport { spawnSync } from \\\"node:child_process\\\";\\nimport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n\\nconst cliPath = path.resolve(\\n  path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)),\\n  \\\"../dist/cli.js\\\",\\n);\\n\\nfunction runBinary(args: string[]): {\\n  status: number | null;\\n  stdout: string;\\n  stderr: string;\\n} {\\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [cliPath, ...args], {\\n    encoding: \\\"utf8\\\",\\n  });\\n  return { status: result.status, stdout: result.stdout, stderr: result.stderr };\\n}\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"FC-0.3 (process boundary): built binary\\\", () => {\\n  it(\\\"dist/cli.js exists (build ran before this suite)\\\", () => {\\n    expect(existsSync(cliPath)).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"--help exits 0 with usage on stdout\\\", () => {\\n    const result = runBinary([\\\"--help\\\"]);\\n    expect(result.status).toBe(0);\\n    expect(result.stdout).toContain(\\\"Usage:\\\");\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"unknown command exits 1 with structured JSON\\\", () => {\\n    const result = runBinary([\\\"nonsense\\\"]);\\n    expect(result.status).toBe(1);\\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(result.stdout) as { ok: boolean };\\n    expect(parsed.ok).toBe(false);\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\\\"a planned command reaches its fail-closed stub through the real binary\\\", () => {\\n    const result = runBinary([\\\"threads\\\", \\\"list\\\"]);\\n    expect(result.status).toBe(1);\\n    expect(JSON.parse(result.stdout)).toEqual({\\n      ok: false,\\n      error: {\\n        errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\",\\n        code: \\\"storage_failure\\\",\\n        reason: \\\"not implemented: threads.list\\\",\\n      },\\n    });\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"numLines\":56,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":56}}}\n577:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" let me run the test typecheck to see the actu