59-62` — moved the `@ts-expect-error` directive down onto the `payload:` line, where the excess-property error actually lands. The directive guarded the `validEvent(...)` line, so it was both unused *and* left the real error unsuppressed.\\n- **Contracts preserved.** The fail-closed CLI stub contract is untouched (no edits to `src/cli/**` or the domain stubs). The discriminated-union compile-time proof is intact — same `@ts-expect-error` assertion, just repositioned so it compiles and still proves an invalid kind/payload pairing requires an explicit cast.\\n- **FC-0.7 proof — ready but blocked on execution.** The Anti-Shim requirement is explicit: the gate self-test must use *real sacrificial files run through the real scripts* — \\\"reviewed as correct\\\" doesn't count. So I can't fake or merely describe it. I wrote `scripts/fc07-gate-self-test.mjs`: one transparent, self-cleaning command that runs the real gates (baseline `verify` → failing-test fails `verify` → unchanged Red file passes `green-verify` → edited Red file fails `green-verify` at the immutability check → clean `verify-all`), records the evidence to an artifact, and restores `red-manifest.json` and removes the sacrificial files via `finally`.\\n\\nI need execution unblocked to actually perform and record the proof.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":503,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":131771,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":503},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7d47137f-cd86-4c15-bbf8-4a8dc794929e\",\"uuid\":\"9682007e-eeeb-4aff-8e9e-83dd0f3c374c\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbubwJc4d4qMmGKThFbT8\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:2122:{\"typ